WEBVTT

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.600
The three separated at a fork in the road.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.740
And now their whereabouts are undisclosed.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.810
Do they want to protect themselves or other people? Or heavenly dreams?

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.770
The creases of disorder are a cauldron of three.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.380
To an endless, eternal picture of hell,

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.570
pushing through time, a door is dispelled.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.510
Your grudge shall be released.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.390
Come on, pass it to me!

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:35.420
Here you go!

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.420
You’re both so good!

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.220
Stop it!

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:47.740
That girl isn’t discussing that Ojou’s possessing her with anyone.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:52.220
She probably thinks no one would believe her.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:55.700
Or maybe, she just doesn’t have anyone to discuss with.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:57.180
Right,

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:01.220
due to her father’s job, apparently she lived alone for a while.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.550
Wind it, Waro-Waro.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.220
Yes, princess.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:01.550
This program is brought to you by Sony Music,

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:04.890
and the listed sponsors.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.460
What? Really?

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.260
I wonder what’s up?

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:12.540
Why not find out?

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.400
Now for the real deal!

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.100
Oh, it’s a recording!

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.820
I wonder if it’s TV? A movie?

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:26.100
Hey! Isn’t that the idol singer Moriyama Jun?

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.380
I hate fate.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.000
Without knowing you were my long-lost brother, I accidentally fell in love with you.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.300
I hate this fate!

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.020
Cut, OK!

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:46.660
That was good, Jun-chan!

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.260
Your acting is almost wasted on your lyrics!

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:51.180
Thank you so much!

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:54.500
She was so cute, Moriyama-chan!

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.500
That’s a real entertainer right there!

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.460
Apparently she’s pretty popular with the older men, too!

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:01.940
Wow, really?

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:05.900
Older men love those kind of serious girls, don’t you think?

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.420
I’m a big fan of yours!

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:16.020
I’ll let you see all of myself!

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:17.930
Please stop!

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:20.410
Someone come!

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:21.660
Someone come quickly!

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:25.260
You bastard, what are you doing?!

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:26.980
Jun!

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:28.530
Are you OK, Jun?

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.000
Y-Yes, boss.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:37.260
We suddenly lost sight of her and were looking for her…

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.660
…And then we heard her scream.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:40.140
You helped us a lot, thank you.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:41.220
No, really…

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.900
We were so enthralled!

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:47.300
I want to thank you in some way… But we’re still shooting…

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:50.660
A reward? Never!

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:51.220
Yeah!

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:57.280
Then, how about we invite them to dinner at the hotel?

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.190
Of course, it’s only if you girls would like to.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:01.660
B-But…

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:02.980
Really? Is it OK?

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:04.100
Sure!

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.420
I’m so nervous!

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.500
We’re probably not going to be able to taste the delicious food!

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:21.860
Hey,

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.660
you girls are going to meet Moriyama Jun now, right?

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.780
Why do you know?

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:30.820
I want you to hand her this.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:36.100
I think she’ll know if you tell her it’s from Momota Masako.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:41.860
First, this is a hors d’œuvre using season vegetables.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.780
Please enjoy.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.340
Go ahead, eat as much as you like!

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:52.100
Yes!

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.020
Time to eat now.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.180
Don’t be so nervous!

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:02.300
Help yourselves!

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:06.140
Y-Yes!

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:08.860
It’s delicious!

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:10.250
Yeah, it’s delicious!

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:15.580
Since Jun is always entertaining regardless of where she is,

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:20.100
she has zero chance to speak with girls of the same age like you.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:24.650
Please relax and speak with Jun.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:29.260
Boss, Yoshizawa-san, my story doesn’t matter;

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:31.860
tonight’s main act is them, right?

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:33.180
Oh, right!

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.060
I’m terribly sorry!

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:40.420
Here you go!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.500
Thank you so much!

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:47.260
Hey, did you know? The part you sign on colored paper is the back!

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.300
Is that true?

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.260
Really?

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:53.540
I’m not important enough to have you sign the front yet;

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:58.260
I’ll work hard and stay devoted-that’s apparently what it means.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:00.500
I had no idea!

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:01.980
You know so much!

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:05.300
Hard work and devotion, eh?

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.860
Jun, I guess you have to work harder, right?

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:09.420
Yes.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:14.020
What? Despite all your popularity, you still need to work harder?

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.420
I have a dream for myself.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:17.740
A dream?

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:19.740
I want my songs,

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:25.580
even after I get old and die, to be sung and passed down.

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:28.030
I’m shooting for that kind of singer.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:31.640
That’s what they call a legendary singer, eh?

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.980
A legendary singer?

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:35.380
It’s beautiful!

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:38.100
Jun-san, you really like singing, don’t you?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.500
It’s not just singing!

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:42.220
You want to say that fans are important too, right?

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:43.020
Right!

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:48.740
Oh I almost forgot!

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:53.750
A woman in front of the hotel told me to give this to you…

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:55.820
Oh, maybe a fan letter?

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:57.580
Let’s see…

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.030
She said that Momota Masako should ring a bell…

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:15.140
What’s this?

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.420
Some people do some horrible pranks!

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:21.530
I mean really…

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:28.260
I love you~

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:30.380
Princess, you’re also good at singing, aren’t you?

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.380
I love…

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:31.360
Yeah!

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:33.420
Take me to the Kan-oke next time!

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:37.000
Kan-oke… You mean Karaoke, right?

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:41.050
Wasn’t that exhausting?

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:45.500
Did you give her that envelope?

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:47.980
Hey, were those pictures real?

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:48.980
You saw them?

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:52.660
Did they say anything?

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:55.830
They said not to tell anybody.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.900
Hmm… And how did you reply?

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:01.100
Of course, we told them we’d stay quiet.

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:06.890
Oh! I’m the same age as her.

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:13.220
We were in the same entertaining office in middle school.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:18.980
This was before she went to her current agent .

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:24.060
It was such a horrible agency! But that wasn’t it.

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:27.700
<i>Hey, Masako,</i>

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:31.100
<i>can you go get me juice from the convenience store?</i>

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.820
<i>I’m sorry, I’m in the middle of a lesson right now.</i>

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:42.580
<i>Who are you talking back to?</i>

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.220
<i>I’m sorry.</i>

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:50.060
<i>Jun-chan, we’ve got a job for you!</i>

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:52.220
<i>Here are the plans an advance.</i>

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:57.260
<i>What? Another photographing event?</i>

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:00.260
<i>At least you have a job.</i>

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:04.420
<i>Why are all my fans so disgusting?</i>

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:07.100
<i>It’s always the same ones anyway!</i>

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:10.220
<i>God, I hate them so much! Really!</i>

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:13.860
<i>Here we go, an erotic pose!</i>

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:22.220
<i>Masako! This time, I’ll take yours for you!</i>

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:22.940
<i>But…</i>

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.820
<i>Come on, come over here!</i>

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:27.060
<i>There!</i>

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:38.420
<i>I’m sorry, that was on purpose!</i>

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:47.460
I gave up my dreams because of her.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:51.940
She trampled my dream of becoming a singer!

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:54.180
I hate Moriyama Jun!

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:58.380
Even if I have to ask Jigoku Shoujo, I want to send her to hell!

00:10:58.380 --> 00:10:59.980
Jigoku Shoujo…

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:11.300
Yes I do! I love you! I love you,

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:18.260
angel on the surfboard! Everyone’s captivated…

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:17.900
Doesn’t she suck?

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:21.900
Hogging all their lines of sight to herself…

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:22.040
You can’t say that! That would be too bad!

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:24.220
You are shining.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:25.940
Masako-san,

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:28.420
what do you want Jun-san to do?

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:31.980
I just want her to apologize to me.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:37.380
If she does that, I could hand over all the photo files.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.660
But, if she doesn’t…

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:40.420
She’s here…

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:56.260
Jun-san…

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.260
Are you satisfied by this?

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:05.980
What pitiful pose!

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:10.900
Right, since if those pictures went public, you wouldn’t be able to stay in show biz,

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:13.980
even if you didn’t want to lower your head, you can.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:17.780
If I said I didn’t feel that way, it would be a lie.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:20.660
But, that’s not all.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:24.300
I was an evil person back then.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:29.500
I finally realized after I broke and met a lot of people.

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:31.580
Don’t say something so rash!

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:33.780
After doing so many bad things to someone,

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:35.860
you want me to forgive you?

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:38.180
How rash can you be?

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:41.900
Then, how…

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:44.940
Hurry and get out of show biz.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:47.660
But that’s different from what you just told us.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.340
If you can’t do that, go die!

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:59.660
Hey, Jun, can you realize my hopes for me?

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:00.820
Hope?

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:04.940
Can you debut me from your agency?

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:09.570
If the ever-popular Moriyama Jun pushed me,

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:13.510
I could quickly become an idol!

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:16.420
I’m sorry, I can’t do that.

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:17.980
Why?

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:23.780
Because… I don’t want to say this, but Masako, you’re bad at singing.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:24.500
That…

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:29.740
It’s true that I bullied you.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.460
I regret that now.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:34.300
But that and this are totally different.

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:38.140
I can now really love singing.

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:39.660
That’s why…

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:43.820
I can’t let an untalented girl debut.

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:45.660
Even I worked hard!

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:51.100
Working hard is what untalented people reach to as their last hope.

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:56.540
Masako, even if you became a singer, you wouldn’t be able to continue.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:02.220
Do whatever you’d like with the pictures.

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:05.300
They’re seeds I sowed by myself, after all.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:07.010
I’ll accept them as my own.

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:23.560
Send

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:20.100
Moriyama Jun

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:20.600
Moriyama Jun

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:20.850
Moriyama Jun

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:20.890
Moriyama Jun

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:21.080
Moriyama Jun

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:23.560
Moriyama Jun

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:28.220
Send

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:28.940
Send

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:30.180
I’m here.

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:41.460
Bone Lady.

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:42.900
Sure, Ojou.

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:49.220
Take this.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:15:00.720
If you really want to release your grudge, you just have to pull the red string.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:05.580
If you pull the string, it would mean you formally signed a contract with me.

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:09.420
The one you grudge will be swiftly sent to hell.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:10.820
But,

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:15.420
if you release it, you’ll have to pay the price.

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:18.100
If you curse one person,

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:23.100
two holes are created. If you sign the contract, your soul will fall to hell, too.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:24.900
Well, that’s only after you die.

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:27.620
To… Hell…

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:33.560
The rest is up to you.

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:52.140
Momota Masako-san, right?

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:55.540
The publishers aren’t coming no matter what.

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:59.140
We won’t do anything if you’d hand that over.

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:05.260
You understand, right?

00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:08.020
I don’t want any involvement with Moriyama Jun.

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:10.820
3 million yen.

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:13.540
You know what I’m saying, right?

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.800
Wow! Moriyama Jun is such an amazing person!

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:24.900
Hey, look over there! Isn’t that the boss of the agency?

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:27.140
I’m going to thank him.

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:27.900
Sure!

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:32.500
They weren’t very pleasant.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:34.940
There was nothing we could do.

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:37.180
Even this is for Jun’s sake.

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.330
Boss.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:39.160
Huh?

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:42.500
For the Agency’s sake, right?

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:44.020
My bad.

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:54.980
You are shining, angel on the surfboard.

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:58.060
I, too, am uneasy.

00:16:58.180 --> 00:17:01.100
I pity myself from not knowing you.

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:05.370
Today, I have something I want to tell all of you.

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:17.420
Before my debut,

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:24.420
I did something horrible to someone else.

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:26.460
J-Jun.

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:32.310
That person won’t forgive me even now.

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:34.760
Jun-san’s talking about it!

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:41.180
The old me was bad.

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:45.220
But I was able to be reborn after I encountered singing.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:49.980
I believe that I was able to meet my real self!

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:51.420
Don’t lose!

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:52.080
Hang in there!

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:53.640
We’re rooting for you!

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:58.620
Thank you! Thank you all!

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:02.300
I can hang on because all of you are here!

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:08.020
I sing this song for that person.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:17.500
To anyone… The sky shines blue.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.500
No… Don’t pull the string!

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:20.420
Don’t pull the string!

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:27.820
Your grudge is released.

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:31.530
Welcome to Enma Ai’s Hell Concert.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.780
W-What? Stop it!

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:24.500
Stop it!

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:27.300
You can’t run away.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:35.300
Even if you’ve changed, your hater still hates you.

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:40.580
She hates her down to her bone marrow.

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:54.780
Trapped in darkness, O pitiful shadow.

00:20:54.780 --> 00:20:57.500
Hurting people, and degrading them.

00:20:57.500 --> 00:21:00.020
Drowned in sin is the ball of karma.

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:06.380
Do you want try dying this once?

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:22.010
I loved you… I loved you…

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:27.900
This hate will send you to hell.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:40.590
We were supposed to have Jun-chan’s concert here.

00:21:41.430 --> 00:21:44.820
Jun… I wonder where she went?

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:49.220
You! From a while back!

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:55.380
I’m sorry about that.

00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:58.340
Hey, you!

00:21:58.460 --> 00:21:59.740
Yoshida, look!

00:22:05.180 --> 00:22:09.420
Moriyama Jun, who disappeared mysteriously.

00:22:05.180 --> 00:22:32.750
Jun-chan… Jun-chan!

00:22:09.420 --> 00:22:15.580
At the hall she was supposed to hold her concert. Many fans are congregating.

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:23.020
Believing that she’ll come back, they continue singing her songs, says many of them.

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:29.020
Jun-san’s dream of becoming a legendary singer,

00:22:29.020 --> 00:22:31.000
maybe it was fulfilled?

00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:41.940
Jun-chan… Jun-chan!

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:41.940
I loved you… I loved you…

00:22:45.180 --> 00:22:49.820
Note: Candle says, Momota Masako.

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:49.820
I’ll release the grudge that you can’t.

00:24:20.940 --> 00:24:21.820
Your name?

00:24:22.490 --> 00:24:23.660
Yukawa Takeru.

00:24:23.660 --> 00:24:25.780
You respected them, no?

00:24:25.780 --> 00:24:28.020
Yeah, I was fond of them.

00:24:28.020 --> 00:24:32.980
That’s why I kept following, and I changed.

00:24:32.980 --> 00:24:35.820
But that something like that would happen…

00:24:35.820 --> 00:24:37.980
even though I believed them!

00:24:37.980 --> 00:24:40.740
Dang it! I’ll send you to hell!

00:24:41.780 --> 00:24:44.100
Your grudge… is granted.

00:24:45.440 --> 00:24:48.700
Next time: Elder Brother.

